<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
<Document>
<Placemark>
<name>Deuxave</name>
<description><![CDATA[<p></p><p><h3><b>Booking Details</b></h3><br/><li><b>Name:</b> Tom Rubel</li><br/><li><b>Date:</b> Sunday, August 2, 2026</li><br/><li><b>Time:</b> 6:30 PM</li><br/><li><b>Party Size:</b> 2 Guests</li><br/><li><b>Confirmation Number:</b> 2109997237 </li><br/><li><b>Restaurant Information</b></li><br/><li><b>Address:</b> 371 Commonwealth Avenue, Boston, MA 02115</li><br/><li><b>Phone:</b> 75175915 <b>Important Policies</b></li><br/><li><b>Grace Period:</b> 15 minutes. You must contact the restaurant if you anticipate being later than this.</li><br/><li><b>Cancellation Policy:</b> Cancellations or no-shows within 24 hours of the reservation will incur a <b>$50 per person</b> charge. Modifying the guest count within 24 hours incurs a <b>$25 per person</b> charge.</li></p><p><h3><b>Description</b></h3></p><p><b>Location:</b> 371 Commonwealth Avenue, Back Bay, Boston, MA  <br/><b>Phone:</b> 617-517-5915 | Hours: Sun-Thu 5pm–9:30pm, Fri 5pm–10pm, Sat 5pm–10:30pm</p><p><h3><b>The Vibe & Atmosphere</b></h3><br/><li><b>Chic elegance without stuffiness.</b>Glamorous chandelier-lit dining room that feels special-occasion-worthy but genuinely welcoming.</li><br/><li><b>Forbes 4-Star rated</b> (retained since 2017); "Best French Restaurant" winner from Boston Magazine multiple times (2014, 2017, 2023, 2025)</li><br/><li>Warm lighting and cream-colored palette with marble & stone accents; windows overlook Commonwealth and Massachusetts Avenues</li><br/><li>Heated outdoor patio (perfect in season); fireplace in main dining room</li><br/><li>Unique feature: <b>wall of mirrors reflecting Back Bay skyline</b></li><br/><li>Beautiful windows framing historic Back Bay architecture</li></p><p><h3><b>The Crowd</b></h3><br/><li>Special occasion diners (celebrations, anniversaries, round-number birthdays)</li><br/><li>Date night couples seeking romance</li><br/><li>Boston's top chefs (professional endorsement—they dine here)</li><br/><li>Upscale but not pretentious clientele</li><br/><li>Mixed business/leisure crowds</li></p><p><h3><b>What Diners Rave About</b></h3></p><p><b>Best Dishes (from reviews):</b><br/><li><b>Duck Confit</b> — Signature dish; crispy exterior, melting meat, often with lentils and Port reduction</li><br/><li><b>Roast Duck</b> — Pistachio-crusted or traditional; called "best duck in the city"</li><br/><li><b>Foie Gras</b> — Luxurious preparations; sometimes paired with prunes soaked in Port</li><br/><li><b>Roast Chicken</b> — Perfectly executed French classic</li><br/><li><b>Crème Brûlée</b> — Coconut version with orange sorbet receives particular praise</li><br/><li><b>Lobster Bisque</b> — Elegant French preparation</li><br/><li><b>Prime Beef Tartare & Wagyu Carpaccio</b> — Described as "ambitious appetizers"</li></p><p><h3><b>Wine Program (Major Strength)</b></h3><br/><li><b>630 selections</b> from 2,600-bottle inventory</li><br/><li><b>Wine Spectator Award of Excellence</b>(since 2015)</li><br/><li>Sommelier <b>Nick Daddona</b> (10+ years experience) curates exceptional pairings</li><br/><li>Specialties: French Burgundy, Bordeaux, Rhône, Bordeaux, Italy, California</li><br/><li>Many bottles under 50;extensive50;extensive100+ selection</li><br/><li>World-class wine program—described as one of Boston's best</li></p><p><h3><b>Service</b></h3><br/><li>Consistently praised as "impeccable," "attentive," and "solicitous"</li><br/><li>Friendly yet professional tone</li><br/><li>Knowledgeable staff about dishes and wine pairings</li><br/><li>Responsive to special occasions</li></p><p><h3><b>Dress Code</b></h3><br/><li>Casual-but-smart to dressy evening wear</li><br/><li>Upscale atmosphere suggests something trendier than business casual</li></p><p><h3><b>What Reviewers Say</b></h3></p><p>> "Exquisite, nouvelle French–inflected cuisine to linger over, beautifully served in a sexy space with a cool bar." — Zagat</p><p>> "Glamorous, chandelier-lit dining room creates special-occasion-feel, but there isn't a hint of stuffiness thanks to friendly vibe." — Time Out</p><p>> "That rare American with a perfect French accent." — Boston Magazine (2025)</p><p><h3><b>To Maximize Your Experience at Deuxave</b></h3></p><p>1. <b>Reserve in advance</b> (8+ parties book via OpenTable as "Experiences"; 13+ via [info@deuxave.com](mailto:info@deuxave.com))<br/>2. <b>Ask for wine pairing recommendations</b> — the sommelier is a major asset<br/>3. <b>Mention occasion</b> — special attention to celebrations/dates<br/>4. <b>Try the seasonal tasting menu</b> (145,addfoiegrassupplementfor 145,addfoiegrassupplementfor 30)<br/>5. <b>Arrive dressed elegantly</b> — the beautiful room invites sophistication<br/>6. <b>Dine in shoulder seasons</b> (spring/early fall) for patio access<br/>7. <b>Consider the duck confit or roast duck</b> as signature dishes<hr/><p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Deuxave/@42.3495174,-71.0916957,812m/data=!3m2!1e3!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x89e37a04c2ac1b6f:0xb67531643a81095!8m2!3d42.3495135!4d-71.0891154!16s%2Fg%2F1tj1t2rv?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYyOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D">View on Google Maps</a></p><p><a href="obsidian://open?vault=Sovereign%20Creator%20OS%20Lite&file=05%20-%20Projects/New%20England%202026/Places/%E2%9C%85%E2%9D%97%EF%B8%8F%E2%9D%8C%20Deuxave">Open in Obsidian</a></p>]]></description>
